/given-names></name><name><surname>Jenkin</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayman</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Oppedisano</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Identification of <italic>Mycobacterium ulcerans</italic> in the environment from regions in Southeast Australia in which it is endemic with sequence capture-PCR.</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><volume>66</volume><fpage>3206</fpage><lpage>3213</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10919771</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000178-Marsollier3"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marsollier</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Stinear</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Aubry</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Saint-Andr&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Robert</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Aquatic plants stimulate the growth of and biofilm formation by <italic>Mycobacterium ulcerans</italic> in axenic culture and harbor these bacteria in the environment.</article-title><source>Appl Environ Microbiol</source><volume>70</volume><fpage>1097</fpage><lpage>1103</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14766593</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000178-Portaels5"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Portaels</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Chemlal</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Elsen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>PDR</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayman</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title><it